IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `scja1-part3-div1`

-- Tests for scja1-part3-div1.l4 (ss 10 to 14). Expected values are written from the text (SCJA1969.txt lines 771-986), not from the code.
-- Weekdays used below, checked against a calendar: 4 January 2026 is a Sunday, so 3 January 2026 is a Saturday, 5 January 2026 a Monday.

§§ `s 10(1): the number of Judges`

#ASSERT `s 10(1) the number of Judges before whom the proceeding is heard and disposed of` NOTHING EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the number of Judges before whom the proceeding is heard and disposed of` (JUST 3) EQUALS 3

§§ `s 10(1A): a direction for more Judges`

-- "any uneven number of Judges greater than the number provided under subsection (1)"
#ASSERT (`s 10(1A) the Chief Justice may direct that the proceeding be heard before this number of Judges` 3 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(1A) the Chief Justice may direct that the proceeding be heard before this number of Judges` 5 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an even number, or not greater than the number under (1): outside the grant, which is silent about them
#ASSERT (`s 10(1A) the Chief Justice may direct that the proceeding be heard before this number of Judges` 2 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 10(1A) the Chief Justice may direct that the proceeding be heard before this number of Judges` 3 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 10(1A) the Chief Justice may direct that the proceeding be heard before this number of Judges` 1 3) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 10(1B): decided by the majority of 3 or more Judges`

#ASSERT `s 10(1B) how a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 2, 1) EQUALS `s 10(1B) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, for the claim, appeal or application`
#ASSERT `s 10(1B) how a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 3, 0) EQUALS `s 10(1B) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, for the claim, appeal or application`
#ASSERT `s 10(1B) how a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 1, 2) EQUALS `s 10(1B) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, against the claim, appeal or application`
#ASSERT `s 10(1B) how a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 2, 3) EQUALS `s 10(1B) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, against the claim, appeal or application`
-- an even division (four Judges, two and two): no majority, the Act does not say
#ASSERT `s 10(1B) how a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 2, 2) EQUALS `s 10(1B) not covered`
-- fewer than 3 Judges: outside the subsection's wording
#ASSERT `s 10(1B) how a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 1, 0) EQUALS `s 10(1B) not covered`
#ASSERT `s 10(1B) how a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 1, 1) EQUALS `s 10(1B) not covered`

§§ `s 10(2): a Judge exercises the jurisdiction`

#ASSERT (`s 10(2) a Judge may exercise the jurisdiction of the General Division in the cause, matter or proceeding` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(2) a Judge may exercise the jurisdiction of the General Division in the cause, matter or proceeding` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(2) a Judge may exercise the jurisdiction of the General Division in the cause, matter or proceeding` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(2) a Judge may exercise the jurisdiction of the General Division in the cause, matter or proceeding` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 10(4): a Judge delivers a reserved judgment after the appointment ends`

#ASSERT (`s 10(4) the Judge has power to deliver judgment despite the expiry or termination of the appointment` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(4) the Judge has power to deliver judgment despite the expiry or termination of the appointment` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10(4) the Judge has power to deliver judgment despite the expiry or termination of the appointment` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 10(5): a Judge who sat as Presiding Judge does not sit on appeals from that office`

#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge must not sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(a) an appeal from a judgment or order made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge must not sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(b) an appeal against a conviction before, or a sentence passed by, the Judge as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge must not sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(c) the consideration of a case stated by the Judge under section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge must not sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(d) an application under section 400 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 in relation to a judgment, order or sentence by the Judge as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge must not sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(e) any proceedings relating to any judgment, order or direction made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a Judge who did not act as the Presiding Judge, or proceedings outside (a) to (e): the subsection does not speak of them
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge must not sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(a) an appeal from a judgment or order made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge must not sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5) another proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The twin for the grant: where the bar applies the Judge may not sit (JUST FALSE); a Judge outside the bar, or a proceeding outside (a) to (e), is not decided.
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge may sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(a) an appeal from a judgment or order made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge may sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(b) an appeal against a conviction before, or a sentence passed by, the Judge as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge may sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(c) the consideration of a case stated by the Judge under section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge may sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(d) an application under section 400 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 in relation to a judgment, order or sentence by the Judge as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge may sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(e) any proceedings relating to any judgment, order or direction made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge may sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5)(a) an appeal from a judgment or order made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 10(5) the Judge may sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` `s 10(5) another proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 10A: assessors`

#ASSERT (`s 10A the court may summon assessors` `General Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10A the court may summon assessors` `General Division` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- reached for the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal through ss 32(3), 50(3)
#ASSERT (`s 10A the court may summon assessors` `Appellate Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10A the court may summon assessors` `Court of Appeal` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a court the section does not name
#ASSERT (`s 10A the court may summon assessors` `Singapore International Commercial Court` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 10A the court may summon assessors` `District Court` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 10A(2) the remuneration of the assessors is costs in the proceedings` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10A(2) the remuneration of the assessors is costs in the proceedings` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10A(2) the remuneration of the assessors is costs in the proceedings` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 10A(3) the remuneration of the assessors is payable out of moneys provided by Parliament` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10A(3) the remuneration of the assessors is payable out of moneys provided by Parliament` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT (`s 10A(4) a party may take objection to the proposed assessor` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10A(4) a party may take objection to the proposed assessor` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10A(4) a party may take objection to the proposed assessor` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 10A(4) a party may take objection to the proposed assessor` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 10B: when the General Division is open`

#ASSERT `s 10B(1) the day is a Saturday` (Date 3 1 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10B(1) the day is a Saturday` (Date 4 1 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10B(1) the day is a Saturday` (Date 5 1 2026))
-- Monday 5 January 2026: sits; Saturday 3 and Sunday 4: does not; a public holiday on a Monday: does not
#ASSERT (`s 10B(1) the General Division is to sit on the day` (Date 5 1 2026) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10B(1) the General Division is to sit on the day` (Date 3 1 2026) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10B(1) the General Division is to sit on the day` (Date 4 1 2026) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10B(1) the General Division is to sit on the day` (Date 12 1 2026) (LIST Date 12 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10B(1) the General Division is to sit on the day` (Date 13 1 2026) (LIST Date 12 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2): a Judge may sit on such a day if the Chief Justice so directs, or the Judge thinks the business extremely urgent
#ASSERT (`s 10B(2) the Judge may lawfully sit on the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10B(2) the Judge may lawfully sit on the day` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 10B(2) the Judge may lawfully sit on the day` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 10B(2) the Judge may lawfully sit on the day` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 11: sittings and distribution of business`

#ASSERT (`s 11(1) the General Division sits at the time and place` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 11(1) the General Division sits at the time and place` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 11(2) the distribution of business among the Judges is as the Act requires` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 11(2) the distribution of business among the Judges is as the Act requires` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 13: enforcement orders for seizure and sale`

-- Wearing apparel, bedding and tools of trade: not seizable up to $1,000 in value; above $1,000 the exception ("when ... does not exceed $1,000") does not apply.
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(a) wearing apparel and bedding of the judgment debtor or the judgment debtor's family, and the tools and implements of the judgment debtor's trade` 1000 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(a) wearing apparel and bedding of the judgment debtor or the judgment debtor's family, and the tools and implements of the judgment debtor's trade` 999 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(a) wearing apparel and bedding of the judgment debtor or the judgment debtor's family, and the tools and implements of the judgment debtor's trade` 1001 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(b) tools of artisans` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) an agriculturist's animals and produce: only those the court thinks necessary for a livelihood.
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(b) an agriculturist's implements of husbandry, and such animals and seed-grain or produce as are necessary to earn a livelihood` 0 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(b) an agriculturist's implements of husbandry, and such animals and seed-grain or produce as are necessary to earn a livelihood` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(c) the wages or salary of the judgment debtor` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(d) a pension, gratuity or allowance granted by the Government` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e) a partnership share the creditor can charge: excepted; one the creditor cannot charge: not within the exception.
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(e) the share of the judgment debtor in a partnership` 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13(e) the share of the judgment debtor in a partnership` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- all other property, movable or immovable, of whatever description
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` TRUE `s 13 property of any other description` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a judgment that is not for the payment of money: the section does not speak of it
#ASSERT (`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` FALSE `s 13 property of any other description` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 14: execution of a deed or indorsement of a negotiable instrument`

#ASSERT (`s 14(1) the interested party may prepare the instrument and tender it to the court for execution` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 14(1) the interested party may prepare the instrument and tender it to the court for execution` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 14(1) the interested party may prepare the instrument and tender it to the court for execution` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 14(1) the Registrar's signature has the same effect as execution by the party ordered` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 14(1) the Registrar's signature has the same effect as execution by the party ordered` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 14(1) the Registrar's signature has the same effect as execution by the party ordered` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 14(1) the Registrar's signature has the same effect as execution by the party ordered` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 14(1) the Registrar's signature has the same effect as execution by the party ordered` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 14(2) section 14 abridges the court's power to proceed by attachment against the person` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 14(2) section 14 abridges the court's power to proceed by attachment against the person` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
